---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site.js';
import { PUBLISHED_ISO, PUBLISHED_LABEL } from '../data/posts.js';

const canonical = `${SITE.url}/privacy/`;
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy | ${SITE.name}`}
  description="What OnwardCraft collects, what it does not, and what happens to your email address if you subscribe."
  canonical={canonical}
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main">
    <div class="container legal">
      <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="legal__date">Last updated <time datetime={PUBLISHED_ISO}>{PUBLISHED_LABEL}</time></p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        This is a blog. We collect an email address if you choose to give us one,
        and anonymous traffic statistics so we know which articles get read.
        That is the entire list.
      </p>

      <h2>Your email address</h2>
      <p>
        If you subscribe to the newsletter, your address is stored so we can send
        it to you. We do not sell it, rent it, share it, or run it through any
        service that tries to work out who you are or where you work. We do not
        add you to any other list. Unsubscribing removes you permanently — there
        is no win-back sequence.
      </p>
      <p>
        Newsletter and contact submissions are delivered through FormSubmit.co,
        which processes the message on its way to us and is subject to its own
        privacy terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics to count page views, referrers and rough
        geography. It sets cookies in your browser. We use it to decide what to
        write next, not to build a profile of you, and we do not run advertising
        or remarketing tags of any kind. Browser-level tracking protection or an
        ad blocker will stop it, and nothing on this site will break if you do.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No advertising networks and no remarketing pixels.</li>
        <li>No selling, renting or trading of any data.</li>
        <li>No accounts, so no passwords and no personal data to leak.</li>
        <li>No payments, so no card details ever touch this site.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Links out</h2>
      <p>
        We link to sources, studies and tools. Those sites have their own privacy
        practices and we have no control over them. None of our outbound links
        are affiliate links.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can unsubscribe from any email in one click, and you can ask us to
        delete your address entirely by writing to <a href="/contact/">the desk</a>.
        We will confirm when it is done.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this notice changes materially, we will update the date at the top and
        say what changed rather than quietly swapping the text.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: 720px; padding: 48px 0 80px; }
  .legal h1 { font-size: clamp(32px, 4.6vw, 46px); margin: 12px 0 10px; }
  .legal__date { font-family: var(--font-ui); font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-3); margin-bottom: 36px; }
  .legal h2 { font-size: 22px; margin: 40px 0 12px; padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .legal p, .legal li {
    font-family: var(--font-read); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .legal p { margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .legal ul { padding-left: 22px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .legal li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .legal li::marker { color: var(--accent); }
  .legal a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
</style>
